  "verifiedStaticFacts": [
    "Each iframe owns a separate authored counter/input/scroll state; initial page labels and zero counters match page-oracle. No storage, external resources, account or Agent operations occur in these pages.",
    "Fixture imports production App with controlled IPC and synthetic threads/drafts. Controlled commands are logged, unsupported commands throw, protected values compared; this is not native backend or installed-product proof.",
    "revision-v2 removes numeric page cap; transport has no page count admission limit. Three pages is coverage, not capacity.",
    "Runner explicitly disclaims native permission/ACK safety and has source hashes plus request/pageerror gates. No browser or server was executed in this review."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "R1",
      "priority": "high-before-claiming-preparation-lifecycle-coverage",
      "path": "output/2026-10-14-browser-tabs-browser/run.mjs",
      "lines": [
        83,
        129
      ],
      "issue": "Current executable runner implements four scenarios only; fixture.configure and release are never invoked. preparation manualScenarios lists ten, including unimplemented failure, late-owner, ABA and task-switch behaviors.",
      "action": "Add scoped scenarios before claiming those behaviors, or explicitly mark them untested. Minimum for frontend runtime-tabs: delayed select completion with no premature show, select/close failure and exact retry ownership, same-page collapse/task-switch retention, pending hidden create across owners, and A-B-A stale result rejection. Native locking and ACK safety remain backend/native proof."
    },
    {
      "id": "R2",
      "priority": "medium-harness-capability",
      "path": "output/2026-10-14-browser-tabs-browser/transport.ts",
      "lines": [
        140,
        146
      ],
      "issue": "release(stage) resolves every held operation of that stage together. It cannot author two owners with reversed native-create completion order.",
      "action": "Permit selecting a held operation by exact label (or return a stable reservation ID) and release only that owner. Exercise C-before-B and B-before-C while late hidden owner cannot steal latest route."
    },
    {
      "id": "R3",
      "priority": "high-evidence-boundary",
      "path": "output/2026-10-14-browser-tabs-browser/transport.ts",
      "lines": [
        117,
        132
      ],
      "issue": "snapshot captures a gate and mock itself throws after revocation; browser_share_allow completes synchronously and has no queued approval capture. Therefore a future snapshot-only test would not prove UI dropping a successfully returned late value or old approval rejection.",
      "action": "Keep mock-rejection scenario separate from a deliberate delayed-success stale-result scenario for the frontend owner check; add held approval with captured original authority if frontend actually owns such pending action. Do not claim backend queued-approval safety from this transport."
    },
    {
      "id": "R4",
      "priority": "medium-oracle-scope",
      "path": "output/2026-10-14-browser-tabs-browser/run.mjs",
      "lines": [
        84,
        128
      ],
      "issue": "A/B memory returns are checked; C assigned memory is not checked on return. page-oracle promises reopening B resets its state, but runner only closes B. Narrow layout checks tablist width and button visibility, not iframe bounds overlapping controls.",
      "action": "At C return verify counter3/noteC/scroll0; reopen closed B and require new identity plus initial state. For non-overlap claim compare iframe rect with toolbar/tablist rect. Otherwise narrow claims to actual checks."
    },
    {
      "id": "R5",
      "priority": "medium-failure-model",
      "path": "output/2026-10-14-browser-tabs-browser/transport.ts",
      "lines": [
        94,
        101
      ],
      "issue": "show failure happens before changing frame display and leaves no global unknown-presentation state in the mock. It can therefore allow later show although oracle-v2 says uncertain visibility stays blocked.",
      "action": "Model an explicit uncertain presentation owner only if testing that frontend error path; keep backend global barrier proof delegated to actual backend tests. A passing mocked show retry alone cannot establish the real safety invariant."
    },
    {
      "id": "R6",
      "priority": "low-wait-precision",
